    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "80334a79_8e0b6f4c",
        "filename": "power/rk3399.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 552,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000407
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-11-15T04:35:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "May rename it having the term \"TABLET\". As it breaks clamshell, which starts a clean shutdown after pressing the power button for 3s. So when holding the power button for 10s. It initiates a power-on again. I think we have rk3399 clamshell, right?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 552,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 552,
        "endChar": 36
      },
      "revId": "fa1e381ef9ff1d36e3805566e58a8615547f1893",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "2b9d936e_7a525400",
        "filename": "power/rk3399.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 552,
      "author": {
        "id": 1148900
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-11-15T06:03:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "power_seq_version 0 is for Kevin/Bob/Gru (clamshell/convertible).\npower_seq_version 1 is for Scarlet rev0. Actually we can clean this up. \npower_seq_version 2 is for Scarlet rev1+.\n\nI think CONFIG_CHIPSET_POWER_SEQ_VERSION is still valuable because we can use this to support multiple different power sequences in one platform. A new config like CONFIG_CHIPSET_POWER_SEQ_TABLET can at most get us one additional power sequence for tablet.",
      "parentUuid": "80334a79_8e0b6f4c",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 552,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 552,
        "endChar": 36
      },
      "revId": "fa1e381ef9ff1d36e3805566e58a8615547f1893",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1e2df12c_20c511a6",
        "filename": "power/rk3399.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
