      "author": {
        "id": 1000407
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-11-15T17:10:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks for explaining.",
      "parentUuid": "2b9d936e_7a525400",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 552,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 552,
        "endChar": 36
      },
      "revId": "fa1e381ef9ff1d36e3805566e58a8615547f1893",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f8087c8a_2101e6f8",
        "filename": "power/rk3399.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 552,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002133
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-11-15T19:45:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e So when holding the power button for 10s. It initiates a power-on again. I think we have rk3399 clamshell, right?\n\nI think this may be a real problem here, right? Don\u0027t tablets also have the behavior in the OS where they do a clean shutdown when you press power for 3s?\n\nSo with this code, if you held the power button until the machine shut off, it would immediately turn on again after release. That seems wrong. I think what you really want is to confirm that chipset_in_state(CHIPSET_STATE_ANY_OFF) is true when the user starts pressing it, and only then power on the machine on release.",
      "parentUuid": "1e2df12c_20c511a6",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 552,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 552,
        "endChar": 36
      },
      "revId": "fa1e381ef9ff1d36e3805566e58a8615547f1893",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "45f157fd_7290c05a",
        "filename": "power/rk3399.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 552,
      "author": {
        "id": 1148900
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-11-15T21:15:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yeah...this will be a problem.\nI\u0027ll fix it.",
      "parentUuid": "f8087c8a_2101e6f8",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 552,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 552,
        "endChar": 36
      },
      "revId": "fa1e381ef9ff1d36e3805566e58a8615547f1893",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f85e8dee_5baab0da",
        "filename": "power/rk3399.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 552,
      "author": {
        "id": 1148900
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-11-15T21:30:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "(To be clear, the tablet clean shutdown is 3s power button press + select \u0027power off\u0027 on the menu. This part is fine. However, the tablet hard shutdown is 10s power button press, which will be a problem since the device would re-boot when power button is released. source: go/crosdebug)",
      "parentUuid": "45f157fd_7290c05a",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 552,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 552,
        "endChar": 36
      },
      "revId": "fa1e381ef9ff1d36e3805566e58a8615547f1893",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "cfe29d54_73be7af8",
        "filename": "power/rk3399.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 552,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000407
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-11-15T21:45:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "When an user presses the power button for 3s, the menu shows up. Most of the users will release the power button and then tap the \"power off\" menu. If they want a force shutdown, they will hold the power button and not tap the menu. I don\u0027t think anyone would still hold pressing the power button and also tap the menu. Do we need to handle this weird use case?",
      "parentUuid": "f85e8dee_5baab0da",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 552,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 552,
        "endChar": 36
      },
      "revId": "fa1e381ef9ff1d36e3805566e58a8615547f1893",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b099f387_9d689f73",
        "filename": "power/rk3399.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 552,
      "author": {
        "id": 1148900
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-11-15T21:56:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Here is the scenario:\n1. 0s: The user press power button\n2. 3s: \u0027power off\u0027 menu pops up, but the user can ignore it and keep holding the power button.\n3. 8s: The devices still shuts off (a.k.a. hard shutdown).\n4. 8+s: The user releases the power button, and then the device boots again!",
      "parentUuid": "cfe29d54_73be7af8",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 552,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 552,
        "endChar": 36
      },
      "revId": "fa1e381ef9ff1d36e3805566e58a8615547f1893",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3dc9bc53_08506532",
        "filename": "power/rk3399.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 552,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002133
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-11-15T22:05:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think it makes sense to be conservative here. We also shouldn\u0027t assume that the current OS behavior will stay that way forever if we can help it. If the user starts pressing the power button while the machine is on and releases it when it is off, then no matter how exactly it got there I think the right thing to do is to stay off.",
      "parentUuid": "b099f387_9d689f73",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 552,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 552,
        "endChar": 36
      },
